Step 0 supports a native Track B family. I’m using the paper’s own \(P_4=H_1\oslash H_2\) objects and Section 3.4’s “bad-edge” decomposition: singleton lists make only one list-pair block obstruct the homomorphism. The generator will compose odd-path obstructions with known alternating deletion sets, while safe edge blocks regularize every vertex’s total degree and create the large mechanical scan. This avoids claiming distributional hardness from the paper’s FPT theorem.
