   216	
   217	## Caveats
   218	
   219	- This is a deliberately restricted singleton-list `P4` family. It exercises
   220	  the paper’s native special-sum/bad-edge mechanism, but it is not evidence
   221	  about arbitrary DL-Hom instances or the open cases in Section 5.
   222	- The mechanical cost measures a standard explicit-edge scan of a graph given
   223	  compactly in blocks. A representation-aware implementation that recognizes
   224	  the same target/list invariant can skip the safe reservoir, which is exactly
   225	  the Track B compression being tested; the family makes no Track A claim.
   226	- The 0/200,000 guess result samples exact-`k` subsets of bad-edge endpoints.
   227	  It excludes safe-only reservoir vertices, but it does not model a solver that
   228	  finds the list-pair decomposition or odd paths.
   229	- Total degree is perfectly regular and obstruction degree does not separate
   230	  all planted vertices from internal decoys. The tested outlier, greedy,
   231	  random-restart, and single-target-side attacks fail. Generic SAT/ILP solvers
   232	  and learned graph heuristics were not tested; Hopcroft–Karp is the successful
   233	  reference algorithm.
   234	- The canonical key handles active renumbering, edge-record order, independent
   235	  reservoir rotations, and reflection through its normalized shift signature.
