codex
Implemented the verified generator as Track B.

Key results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- Planted witnesses verify for 12/12 preset/seed combinations.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four heuristic attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference Hopcroft–Karp/Kőnig algorithm: 8/8, averaging 1,649 operations.
- Answer cap: 673 characters, 96 atoms.
- Intended route: at most 236 operations.

Track B is required because Theorem 1.1 proves FPT for skew-decomposable targets, and Lemma 3.22 supplies the bad-edge branching mechanism. [Paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1308.1068).

Deliverables:

- [gen_1308_1068.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1308.1068/gen_1308_1068.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1308.1068/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1308.1068/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1308.1068/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1308.1068/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1308.1068/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The only blocker is external: every oracle call returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” Consequently, all three arms have zero valid attempts and the family is locally verified but not yet shippable. Restore the OpenRouter quota, then rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/1308.1068
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1308_1068.py
```
